    "https://dal.peopleadmin.ca/postings/21985": {
      "title": "Dalhousie University | Research Technician",
      "description": "Dalhousie University | Research Technician Skip to Main Content JOBS AT DALHOUSIE UNIVERSITY Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About Dalhousie The Dalhousie Impact Working at Dal Equity, Diversity and Inclusion Talent Pathways Student Employment Hiring a Student FAQS for applicants Research Technician Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Research Technician Research Project Marine Biogeochemistry Laboratory Department/Unit Oceanography Location Halifax, Nova Scotia, Canada Posting Number S232-26 Employee Group Grant-Paid (PSAC Local 86001) Position Type Term Duration of Contract (if applicable) 1 year with possibility of extension Employment Type Full Time Full-time Equivalency (FTE) 1.0 Salary $53,469 - $67,685 per annum at 37.5 hours per week Classification Provisional Statement About Dalhousie University Dalhousie University is Atlantic Canada’s leading research-intensive university and a driver of the region’s intellectual, social and economic development. Located in the heart of Halifax, Nova Scotia, with an Agricultural Campus in Truro/Bible Hill, Dalhousie is a truly national and international university, with more than half of our almost 21,000 students coming from outside of the province. Our 6,000 faculty and staff foster a vibrant, purpose-driven community, that celebrated 200 years of academic excellence in 2018. Job Summary Reporting to the Principal Investigators, the Research Technician will manage the shared marine biogeochemistry laboratory of the Principal Investigators. Responsibilities include laboratory operations and inventory management, maintenance and calibration of scientific instrumentation, health and safety compliance, training colleagues , conducting field sampling, and performing chemical and biogeochemical analyses of environmental samples. The position plays a key role in supporting a diverse portfolio of marine research projects and ensuring the smooth operation of the laboratory. Key Responsibilities Coordinate the day-to-day operations of a shared research laboratory, ensuring efficient workflows, organization, and compliance with safety and regulatory requirements. Manage laboratory resources, including inventory, procurement, equipment maintenance, servicing coordination, and shared equipment scheduling. Support research activities through experimental setup, data collection and management, fieldwork participation, and assistance with multiple concurrent projects. Train and onboard students, staff, and visitors on laboratory techniques, instrumentation, safety procedures, and best practices. Provide administrative support by managing budgets, purchases, expense tracking, compliance documentation, and grant-related reporting requirements. Foster collaboration across research groups by serving as a central point of contact, promoting effective communication, equitable use of shared resources, and a positive laboratory culture. Note Incumbent must have a valid driver’s license and passport and be able to travel internationally. Due to operational requirements, the successful applicant is required to work in-person on campus. Required Qualifications Undergraduate degree in a relevant scientific field (e.g., oceanography, geology, biology, chemistry or related discipline) Strong organizational and problem-solving skills. Experience with laboratory safety standards and compliance. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Have the physical stamina to conduct work at sea (e.g., stand for long periods of time on a moving deck to potentially adverse weather conditions, be able to lift and carry loads of approximately 20 kgs multiple times in a working day). Assets Master’s field in a relevant field. Analytical chemistry experience. Prior experience in a lab manager or supervisory role. Experience with budgeting, ordering systems, and inventory software. Experience supporting multiple research groups or shared facilities. Prior sea going experience. Job Competencies The successful candidate is expected to demonstrate proficiency in Dalhousie’s core and leadership competencies, in particular: - Respect & Inclusion - Adaptability - Knowledge & Thinking Skills - Communication - Service Additional Information Dalhousie University supports a healthy and balanced lifestyle. Our total compensation package includes a voluntary RRSP , health and dental plans, a wellness allowance, an employee and family assistance program and a tuition assistance program. Application Consideration Non-probationary bargaining unit employees ( PSAC Local 86001) are given priority consideration. All other applications will be considered when there is no qualified candidate from the bargaining unit. Full-time students currently enrolled at an educational institution are not eligible for regular Grant-Paid positions. We sincerely appreciate all applications and note that only candidates selected for an interview will be contacted directly by the hiring department or People and Culture. Diversity Statement Dalhousie University commits to achieving inclusive excellence through continually championing equity, diversity, inclusion, and accessibility. The university encourages applications from Indigenous Peoples of Turtle Island (especially Mi’kmaq), persons of Black/African descent (especially African Nova Scotians), and members of other racialized groups, persons with disabilities, women, persons identifying as members of 2SLGBTQIA+ communities, and all candidates who would contribute to the diversity of our community. In accordance with our Employment Equity Policy, preference will be given in hiring processes to candidates who self-identify as members of one or more of the equity-deserving groups listed above. For more information, including details related to our Employment Equity Policy and Plan and definitions of equity-deserving groups please review our Employment Equity information. If you require any support for the purpose of accommodation, such as technical aids or alternative arrangements, please let us know of these needs and how we can be of assistance. Dalhousie University is committed to ensuring all candidates have full, fair, and equitable participation in the hiring process. Our complete Accommodation Policy can be viewed here . Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 1 Open Date 08/10/2026 Close Date 09/04/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicant Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://dal.peopleadmin.ca/postings/21777 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Résumé / Curriculum Vitae (CV) Optional Documents Cover Letter Dalhousie University Halifax, Nova Scotia, Canada  B3H 4R2 1-902-494-2211 Agricultural Campus Truro, Nova Scotia, Canada  B2N 5E3 1-902-893-6600 Contact Us | Campus Directory | Campus Maps Media Centre | Privacy Statement Terms of Use To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
