    "https://dal.peopleadmin.ca/postings/22107": {
      "title": "Dalhousie University | Postdoctoral Fellow – Aging and Care in the Context of Extreme Events",
      "description": "Dalhousie University | Postdoctoral Fellow – Aging and Care in the Context of Extreme Events Skip to Main Content JOBS AT DALHOUSIE UNIVERSITY Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About Dalhousie The Dalhousie Impact Working at Dal Equity, Diversity and Inclusion Talent Pathways Student Employment Hiring a Student FAQS for applicants Postdoctoral Fellow – Aging and Care in the Context of Extreme Events Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Postdoctoral Fellow – Aging and Care in the Context of Extreme Events Posting Number PTAP3537P Department/Unit Social Work Location Halifax, Nova Scotia, Canada Job Summary & Key Responsibilities A postdoctoral fellow ( PDF ) position is available in the Building a Culture of Resilience (BaCoR) lab, led by Professor Haorui Wu, Canada Research Chair (Tier 2) in Resilience, within the School of Social Work, Faculty of Health, Dalhousie University, Halifax, Nova Scotia, Canada. Position The PDF will support a range of interdisciplinary research projects examining the social, health, and policy dimensions of aging across Canada and internationally. These projects include, but are not limited to: Aging in place and continuity of care in the context of extreme events. Experiences of older adults, family caregivers, and migrant care workers within changing health care, social service, and immigration systems. Psychosocial impacts of extreme events, displacement, social isolation, and care disruption on older adults. Key Responsibilities Design and implement quantitative, qualitative, and mixed-methods research. Manage and coordinating research projects. Analyze quantitative and qualitative data; communicating research outcomes to diverse audiences. Prepare findings for scholarly publications. Depending on qualifications and experience, the successful candidate may co-develop research grant applications directly aligned with the lab’s research agenda, strengthen their professional network through collaborations with public, private, and not-for-profit sectors, prepare policy briefs and knowledge mobilization products, and co-supervise undergraduate and graduate students, among other responsibilities. The PDF will be well-positioned to flourish in an innovative, interdisciplinary, and stakeholder-engaged research environment by bringing flexibility, self-motivation, attention to detail, and the ability to manage multiple tasks efficiently, while contributing as a collaborative team member. The successful candidate will join an interdisciplinary network spanning institutions across Canada, the United States, Europe, and other international settings. Participation in academic career development programs offered by Dalhousie University is encouraged. The PDF will be employed by Dalhousie University (www.dal.ca) and must be physically based in Halifax, Nova Scotia. Start date: Anticipated November 1, 2026. Earlier start dates may be considered, and candidates are encouraged to begin as soon as possible. Deadline for application: Review of applications is on an ongoing basis, and applications will be accepted until September 30, 2026. For further information, please contact Dr. Szymon Parzniewski: s.parzniewski@dal.ca Qualifications/Requirements of Position A doctoral degree by the appointment start date in a relevant field, such as Psychology, Gerontology, Public Health, Migration Studies, Social Work, Sociology, or related research areas Demonstrated proficiency in quantitative and qualitative research design, data analysis and interpretation, knowledge mobilization and ability to contribute to community-engaged research Strong record of scholarly writing and peer-reviewed publications, as well as excellent oral communication skills for academic, professional, policy, and public audiences. Evidence of project management experience, including coordination of research activities, support for students and staff, and management of timelines, budgets and other project resources. Experience working in diverse and multicultural environments, with demonstrated cultural humility, intercultural competence, and the ability to work effectively both independently and collaboratively within interdisciplinary teams and community partnerships. To apply for the position, please submit the following documents through Dalhousie University’s online application system. 1. Cover Letter (max. 2 pages) outlining your suitability for the role and addressing the required qualifications 2. Résumé / Curriculum Vitae (CV) 3. Two peer-reviewed publications 4. Academic transcript of the doctoral program (non-official copies are acceptable) 5. List of Referees Contact information (including email addresses) for three references. We thank all applicants; however, only completed applications will be considered, and only candidates selected for an interview will be contacted. Salary Range/Pay Rate $52,000 to $70,000 CAD, commensurate with qualifications and experience Additional Information Dalhousie University commits to achieving inclusive excellence through continually championing equity, diversity, inclusion, and accessibility. The university encourages applications from Indigenous Peoples of Turtle Island (especially Mi’kmaq), persons of Black/African descent (especially African Nova Scotians), and members of other racialized groups, persons with disabilities, women, persons identifying as members of 2SLGBTQIA+ communities, and all candidates who would contribute to the diversity of our community. In accordance with our Employment Equity Policy, preference will be given in hiring processes to candidates who self-identify as members of one or more of the equity-deserving groups listed above. For more information, including details related to our Employment Equity Policy and Plan and definitions of equity-deserving groups please review our Employment Equity information. If you require any support for the purpose of accommodation, such as technical aids or alternative arrangements, please let us know of these needs and how we can be of assistance. Dalhousie University is committed to ensuring all candidates have full, fair, and equitable participation in the hiring process. Our complete Accommodation Policy can be viewed here . Posting Detail Information Term of appointment 1 year with a 6-month probationary period, anticipated start date of November 1, 2026 Open Date 08/31/2026 Close Date 09/30/2026 Open Until Filled No Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://dal.peopleadmin.ca/postings/22092 Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Résumé / Curriculum Vitae (CV) Sample Publication(s) List of referees Transcripts Optional Documents Dalhousie University Halifax, Nova Scotia, Canada  B3H 4R2 1-902-494-2211 Agricultural Campus Truro, Nova Scotia, Canada  B2N 5E3 1-902-893-6600 Contact Us | Campus Directory | Campus Maps Media Centre | Privacy Statement Terms of Use To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://dal.peopleadmin.ca/postings/22046": {
      "title": "Dalhousie University | Director, Industry Partnerships",
      "description": "Dalhousie University | Director, Industry Partnerships Skip to Main Content JOBS AT DALHOUSIE UNIVERSITY Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About Dalhousie The Dalhousie Impact Working at Dal Equity, Diversity and Inclusion Talent Pathways Student Employment Hiring a Student FAQS for applicants Director, Industry Partnerships Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Director, Industry Partnerships Research Project Department/Unit Dal Partners Location Halifax, Nova Scotia, Canada Posting Number S264-26 Employee Group DPMG Position Type Term Duration of Contract (if applicable) 2.5 years Employment Type Full Time Full-time Equivalency (FTE) 1.0 Salary $82,887 - $111,181 per annum, 35 hours per week Classification ADM-07 Provisional Statement This is a provisional classification. Formal regular review classification procedures may be initiated at any time by the incumbent or supervisor after the incumbent has worked a minimum of six months in the role. About Dalhousie University Dalhousie University is Atlantic Canada’s leading research-intensive university and a driver of the region’s intellectual, social and economic development. Located in the heart of Halifax, Nova Scotia, with an Agricultural Campus in Truro/Bible Hill, Dalhousie is a truly national and international university, with more than half of our almost 21,000 students coming from outside of the province. Our 6,000 faculty and staff foster a vibrant, purpose-driven community, that celebrated 200 years of academic excellence in 2018. Job Summary Dalhousie University, under the leadership of the Vice-President Research & Innovation, administers more than $270 million in research funding annually. Reporting to the Managing Director, Dal Partners, the Director, Industry Partnership leads strategic partnerships that connect Dalhousie University ’s research strengths with industry, government, and innovation partners. The Director advances sponsored research, talent development, and economic impact, serving as a bridge between the university and external stakeholders. Key Responsibilities Lead the development and execution of strategic partnership and business development initiatives that advance Dalhousie’s research, innovation, and institutional priorities. Lead and advance high-value partnership opportunities with industry, government, and innovation ecosystem organizations by representing Dalhousie externally and driving cross-university collaboration to grow sponsored research, support institutional priorities, and strengthen the university’s impact and reach. Negotiate and execute complex partnership agreements, collaborating with faculty, researchers, and internal stakeholders to achieve successful outcomes. Manage and grow a portfolio of strategic partner accounts, strengthening relationships and expanding opportunities across research, talent, and philanthropic initiatives. Serve as a senior relationship manager for a portfolio of strategic accounts, building trusted partnerships with executives, researchers, government leaders, and funding organizations. Convene and coordinate faculty, researchers, and institutional leaders to develop compelling partnership opportunities that align external needs with Dalhousie’s strengths. Note The successful applicant will be eligible for hybrid work (combination of in-person work on campus and remote work from within Nova Scotia) as agreed by all parties based on operational requirements and university guidelines. Required Qualifications Undergraduate degree, plus approximately five to seven years’ of related experience (or an equivalent combination of training and experience). Demonstrated experience in business development, strategic partnerships, corporate engagement, government relations, innovation, account management, sponsored research, technology commercialization, or related external-facing roles. Demonstrated ability to originate, negotiate, and successfully close complex, high-value partnership agreements. Demonstrated relationship management skills with the ability to build trust and influence senior internal and external stakeholders. Demonstrated understanding of, or ability to quickly learn, research funding programs and university-industry partnership models. Excellent communication, strategic planning, and portfolio management skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities and opportunities simultaneously. Assets Master’s degree in relevant field. Job Competencies The successful candidate is expected to demonstrate proficiency in Dalhousie’s core and leadership competencies, in particular: - Self-Awareness & Professionalism - Integrity - Respect & Inclusion - Adaptability - Knowledge & Thinking Skills Additional Information Dalhousie University supports a healthy and balanced lifestyle. Our total compensation package includes a defined benefit pension plan, health and dental plans, a health spending account, an employee and family assistance program and a tuition assistance program. Application Consideration Applications from current university employees and external candidates are assessed concurrently. Current university employees will be given special consideration. We sincerely appreciate all applications and note that only candidates selected for an interview will be contacted directly by the hiring department or People and Culture. Diversity Statement Dalhousie University commits to achieving inclusive excellence through continually championing equity, diversity, inclusion, and accessibility. The university encourages applications from Indigenous Peoples of Turtle Island (especially Mi’kmaq), persons of Black/African descent (especially African Nova Scotians), and members of other racialized groups, persons with disabilities, women, persons identifying as members of 2SLGBTQIA+ communities, and all candidates who would contribute to the diversity of our community. In accordance with our Employment Equity Policy, preference will be given in hiring processes to candidates who self-identify as members of one or more of the equity-deserving groups listed above. For more information, including details related to our Employment Equity Policy and Plan and definitions of equity-deserving groups please review our Employment Equity information. If you require any support for the purpose of accommodation, such as technical aids or alternative arrangements, please let us know of these needs and how we can be of assistance. Dalhousie University is committed to ensuring all candidates have full, fair, and equitable participation in the hiring process. Our complete Accommodation Policy can be viewed here . Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 1 Open Date 08/19/2026 Close Date 09/03/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicant Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://dal.peopleadmin.ca/postings/21975 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Résumé / Curriculum Vitae (CV) Optional Documents Cover Letter Dalhousie University Halifax, Nova Scotia, Canada  B3H 4R2 1-902-494-2211 Agricultural Campus Truro, Nova Scotia, Canada  B2N 5E3 1-902-893-6600 Contact Us | Campus Directory | Campus Maps Media Centre | Privacy Statement Terms of Use To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
