    "https://dal.peopleadmin.ca/postings/22106": {
      "title": "Dalhousie University | Administrative Assistant",
      "description": "Dalhousie University | Administrative Assistant Skip to Main Content JOBS AT DALHOUSIE UNIVERSITY Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About Dalhousie The Dalhousie Impact Working at Dal Equity, Diversity and Inclusion Talent Pathways Student Employment Hiring a Student FAQS for applicants Administrative Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Administrative Assistant Research Project Department/Unit Undergraduate Medical Education Location Halifax, Nova Scotia, Canada Posting Number S283-26 Employee Group NSGEU Local 77 Position Type Term Duration of Contract (if applicable) 1 year Employment Type Full Time Full-time Equivalency (FTE) 1.0 Salary $27.60 - $34.94 per hour ($50,232–$63,584 per annum, 35 hours per week) Classification C5 Provisional Statement This is a provisional classification. Formal regular review classification procedures may be initiated at any time by the incumbent or supervisor after the incumbent has worked a minimum of six months in the role. About Dalhousie University Dalhousie University is Atlantic Canada’s leading research-intensive university and a driver of the region’s intellectual, social and economic development. Located in the heart of Halifax, Nova Scotia, with an Agricultural Campus in Truro/Bible Hill, Dalhousie is a truly national and international university, with more than half of our almost 21,000 students coming from outside of the province. Our 6,000 faculty and staff foster a vibrant, purpose-driven community, that celebrated 200 years of academic excellence in 2018. Job Summary The Department of Undergraduate Medical Education ( UGME ) within the Faculty of Medicine, delivers an informative and challenging curriculum for the undergraduate students enrolled in the Medical School, which will prepare them for the next stage of their medical education. Reporting to the Manager, Academic Progress, the Administrative Assistant will provide administrative support for the UGME office, Assistant Dean and various committees as well as be the primary contact for the department. Key Responsibilities Serve as the primary administrative contact for Undergraduate Medical Education ( UGME ), managing student, faculty, and stakeholder communications while ensuring accurate tracking of student records, attendance, and program requirements. Coordinate and support UGME committees by scheduling meetings, preparing agendas and materials, recording and distributing minutes, maintaining documentation, and ensuring follow-up on action items. Provide executive administrative support to UGME leadership, including managing calendars, correspondence, meeting preparation, inquiries, and confidential information. Administer student-related processes, including requests for time off, absence tracking, certification monitoring, records management, and communication of decisions in accordance with established policies and procedures. Deliver office administration and reception services, including responding to inquiries, managing office operations, maintaining supplies and budgets, processing payments, distributing mail, and supporting departmental initiatives. Maintain accurate electronic and physical records, prepare routine correspondence and reports, assist with examinations and data entry, and contribute to the implementation of process improvements and administrative best practices. Note The successful applicant will be eligible for hybrid work (combination of in-person work on campus and remote work from within Nova Scotia) as agreed by all parties based on operational requirements and university guidelines. Required Qualifications Business Administration or Administrative Professional program with three to five years’ relevant experience (or an equivalent combination of training and experience). Demonstrated excellence in organizational, communication, interpersonal, and customer service skills, with strong attention to detail and accuracy. Advanced proficiency in Microsoft Office applications, including Word, Excel, PowerPoint, and SharePoint, with strong data entry and records management skills. Proven ability to work independently, manage multiple competing priorities, exercise sound judgment, and maintain confidentiality with professionalism and discretion. Assets Experience working in a university, healthcare, government, or academic medical education environment. Knowledge of records management practices, committee administration, and meeting coordination. Familiarity with medical education programs, regulatory reporting processes, and stakeholder engagement across academic and healthcare organizations. Job Competencies The successful candidate is expected to demonstrate proficiency in Dalhousie’s core competencies, in particular: - Respect & Inclusion - Adaptability - Knowledge & Thinking Skills - Communication - Service Additional Information Dalhousie University supports a healthy and balanced lifestyle. Our total compensation package includes a defined benefit pension plan, health and dental plans, a health spending account, an employee and family assistance program and a tuition assistance program. Application Consideration Non-probationary bargaining unit employees ( NSGEU local 77) are given priority consideration. All other applications will be considered when there is no qualified candidate from the bargaining unit. We sincerely appreciate all applications and note that only candidates selected for an interview will be contacted directly by the hiring department or People and Culture. Diversity Statement Dalhousie University commits to achieving inclusive excellence through continually championing equity, diversity, inclusion, and accessibility. The university encourages applications from Indigenous Peoples of Turtle Island (especially Mi’kmaq), persons of Black/African descent (especially African Nova Scotians), and members of other racialized groups, persons with disabilities, women, persons identifying as members of 2SLGBTQIA+ communities, and all candidates who would contribute to the diversity of our community. In accordance with our Employment Equity Policy, preference will be given in hiring processes to candidates who self-identify as members of one or more of the equity-deserving groups listed above. For more information, including details related to our Employment Equity Policy and Plan and definitions of equity-deserving groups please review our Employment Equity information. If you require any support for the purpose of accommodation, such as technical aids or alternative arrangements, please let us know of these needs and how we can be of assistance. Dalhousie University is committed to ensuring all candidates have full, fair, and equitable participation in the hiring process. Our complete Accommodation Policy can be viewed here . Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 1 Open Date 08/28/2026 Close Date 09/04/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicant Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://dal.peopleadmin.ca/postings/22073 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Résumé / Curriculum Vitae (CV) Optional Documents Cover Letter Dalhousie University Halifax, Nova Scotia, Canada  B3H 4R2 1-902-494-2211 Agricultural Campus Truro, Nova Scotia, Canada  B2N 5E3 1-902-893-6600 Contact Us | Campus Directory | Campus Maps Media Centre | Privacy Statement Terms of Use To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://dal.peopleadmin.ca/postings/22010": {
      "title": "Dalhousie University | Associate Legal Counsel, Research &amp; Innovation",
      "description": "Dalhousie University | Associate Legal Counsel, Research &amp; Innovation Skip to Main Content JOBS AT DALHOUSIE UNIVERSITY Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About Dalhousie The Dalhousie Impact Working at Dal Equity, Diversity and Inclusion Talent Pathways Student Employment Hiring a Student FAQS for applicants Associate Legal Counsel, Research & Innovation Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Associate Legal Counsel, Research & Innovation Research Project Department/Unit Research Services Location Halifax, Nova Scotia, Canada Posting Number S237-26 Employee Group DPMG Position Type Regular, On-Going Duration of Contract (if applicable) Employment Type Full Time Full-time Equivalency (FTE) 1.0 Salary $82,887 - $111,181 per annum, 35 hours per week Classification ADM-07 Provisional Statement This is a provisional classification. Formal regular review classification procedures may be initiated at any time by the incumbent or supervisor after the incumbent has worked a minimum of six months in the role. About Dalhousie University Dalhousie University is Atlantic Canada’s leading research-intensive university and a driver of the region’s intellectual, social and economic development. Located in the heart of Halifax, Nova Scotia, with an Agricultural Campus in Truro/Bible Hill, Dalhousie is a truly national and international university, with more than half of our almost 21,000 students coming from outside of the province. Our 6,000 faculty and staff foster a vibrant, purpose-driven community, that celebrated 200 years of academic excellence in 2018. Job Summary Dalhousie University administers more than $270 million in annual research funding. Reporting to the Vice-President, Research and Innovation and working under the guidance of the Senior Associate Legal Counsel, the Associate Legal Counsel provides legal advice on research and innovation matters, including research agreements, intellectual property, regulatory compliance, and commercialization. The Associate Legal Counsel supports one of Canada’s leading research-intensive universities at the intersection of law, research, health, and innovation. Key Responsibilities Provide legal advice and support on contracts and agreements, intellectual property, commercialization, confidentiality, data use and other legal issues arising from research and innovation activities. Provide legal advice and guidance to researchers and Research & Innovation staff on research agreements, intellectual property, compliance, and related matters. Support the administration of research contracts, including advising on contractual obligations, account setup, reporting requirements, and contract compliance. Assist in the development, review, and implementation of research-related policies and procedures under the guidance of senior legal counsel. Collaborate with internal and external stakeholders, including researchers, university administrators, funding agencies, industry partners, and legal counsel to facilitate research agreements and resolve issues. Contribute to legal projects and initiatives within the Research & Innovation portfolio and maintain awareness of relevant legal and regulatory developments affecting university research. Note The successful applicant will be eligible for hybrid work (combination of in-person work on campus and remote work from within Nova Scotia) as agreed by all parties based on operational requirements and university guidelines. Required Qualifications Bachelor of Laws ( LLB ), Juris Doctor (JD), or equivalent law degree, together with a minimum of two years’ experience practising law. Practicing member in good standing of the Barrister’s Society of Nova Scotia, or eligible to become a practicing member. Demonstrated knowledge of intellectual property law and related legal issues. Demonstrated experience negotiating, reviewing and advising on contracts and agreements, advising stakeholders on contractual terms, obligations and risks. Demonstrated experience in the development, implementation, and review of policies. Demonstrated ability to exercise sound legal judgment, assess risk and provide practical, solutions-oriented legal advice to a range of stakeholders. Demonstrated ability to build effective working relationships and communicate complex legal issues clearly to researchers, administrators, institutional leaders and external partners, through exceptional communication skills (written and oral) in a fast-paced environment. Assets Experience working in a university, research or innovation environment. Experience with research agreements, clinical/health research or research involving human participants. Familiarity with research ethics and regulatory frameworks. Experience with privacy and data protection law. Experience with intellectual property, commercialization or technology transfer. Job Competencies The successful candidate is expected to demonstrate proficiency in Dalhousie’s core and leadership competencies, in particular: - Integrity - Respect & Inclusion - Adaptability - Knowledge & Thinking Skills - Communication Additional Information Dalhousie University supports a healthy and balanced lifestyle. Our total compensation package includes a defined benefit pension plan, health and dental plans, a health spending account, an employee and family assistance program and a tuition assistance program. Application Consideration Applications from current university employees and external candidates are assessed concurrently. Current university employees will be given special consideration. We sincerely appreciate all applications and note that only candidates selected for an interview will be contacted directly by the hiring department or People and Culture. Diversity Statement Dalhousie University commits to achieving inclusive excellence through continually championing equity, diversity, inclusion, and accessibility. The university encourages applications from Indigenous Peoples of Turtle Island (especially Mi’kmaq), persons of Black/African descent (especially African Nova Scotians), and members of other racialized groups, persons with disabilities, women, persons identifying as members of 2SLGBTQIA+ communities, and all candidates who would contribute to the diversity of our community. In accordance with our Employment Equity Policy, preference will be given in hiring processes to candidates who self-identify as members of one or more of the equity-deserving groups listed above. For more information, including details related to our Employment Equity Policy and Plan and definitions of equity-deserving groups please review our Employment Equity information. If you require any support for the purpose of accommodation, such as technical aids or alternative arrangements, please let us know of these needs and how we can be of assistance. Dalhousie University is committed to ensuring all candidates have full, fair, and equitable participation in the hiring process. Our complete Accommodation Policy can be viewed here . Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 1 Open Date 08/13/2026 Close Date 09/03/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicant Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://dal.peopleadmin.ca/postings/21798 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Résumé / Curriculum Vitae (CV) Optional Documents Cover Letter Dalhousie University Halifax, Nova Scotia, Canada  B3H 4R2 1-902-494-2211 Agricultural Campus Truro, Nova Scotia, Canada  B2N 5E3 1-902-893-6600 Contact Us | Campus Directory | Campus Maps Media Centre | Privacy Statement Terms of Use To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
